    docs(ops): BUNKER_SERVER is not optional — the runbook's "unless --server" branch does not exist (CF-167)
    
    docs/OPERATIONS.md §6 step 3 told the operator "Required environment:
    BUNKER_SERVER unless --server is supplied", and §11 listed the verify-node
    invocation with no environment precondition. The shipped script has no such
    branch: scripts/verify-node.sh:17 assigns
      SERVER="${BUNKER_SERVER:?set BUNKER_SERVER to your bunker server name}"
    in a plain assignment, so the shell expands that guard while executing line 17,
    before the argument loop at :18-26 reads argv (--server is :21). The flag can
    only overwrite a name the environment already supplied.
    
    Measured this tick, two arms with opposite structures:
      $ env -u BUNKER_SERVER ./scripts/verify-node.sh --agent probe-agent \
          --server some-server --port 10800
      ./scripts/verify-node.sh: line 17: BUNKER_SERVER: set BUNKER_SERVER to your bunker server name
      rc=1                      # never prints its own "verify node <id>" banner
      $ BUNKER_SERVER=some-server ./scripts/verify-node.sh --agent probe-agent \
          --server some-server --port 10800
      verify node probe-agent
      FAIL agent_alive — bunker: server "some-server" not found in config
                                # reaches the first probe, i.e. the flag is read
                                  only after the env guard
    
    The corrected prose states the shipped contract, cites :17 and :18-26, and
    names CF-063 as the row that owns relaxing the guard, so the sentence stops
    documenting an intention as behaviour. §11's boundary cell carries the same
    requirement, because that table is what an operator greps when the recipe is
    not at hand.
    
    Evidence: docs/audits/code-factory-docs-2026-11-04-verify-env.md — before/after
    table with file:line, the code path, both arm transcripts, the claims I could
    not verify, and the gate section.
    
    Board: files CF-167 (pending at this commit; closed by the follow-up closeout
    commit that binds this SHA and the CF-167-DOC2 verdict). The row carries the
    probe this commit's evidence quotes.
    
    Transport: this work ran in a fresh clone of the published ref (gh/main
    9b7fb6f) because the registered checkout /home/kara/code-factory held sibling
    lanes mid-tick (code-factory-pm and code-factory-duckbrain-releng both
    `running`, one with docs/audits/code-factory-releng-2026-11-04-CF-163-AC3.md
    staged) plus stale REBASE_HEAD metadata from a completed rebase. The registered
    checkout was not written to.
    
    Guard position, stated rather than implied: this clone has no installed
    pre-commit hook (`core.hooksPath` empty, no .git/hooks/pre-commit), so no hook
    ran and none is claimed. The guard battery runs through
    `gitreins task complete CF-167-DOC2` against this commit.
    
    Gate: at the selection tip (gh/main 9b7fb6f) the suite was RED — `SELFTEST:
    FAIL (1)` with two `FAIL audit-scope` rows naming
    docs/audits/code-factory-releng-2026-11-04-CF-163-AC3.md:39 and :77, a sibling
    lane's file and not this diff (reproduced in a detached worktree of 9b7fb6f
    with zero porcelain). That gate was repaired mid-tick by a sibling landing,
    8995064 "docs(releng): restore the audit-scope gate on the published tip
    (CF-163 AC3)"; this commit was rebased onto 92cfee9 and the gate re-ran GREEN
    at the rebased head: `SELFTEST: PASS` rc 0, `PASS 141/141 rows parse`.
    `bash scripts/boardctl validate` -> RESULT: OK (3 warning(s), both pre-existing:
    CF-034 free-form guard/ci prose and the headerless board). Both runs are
    transcribed in the evidence file's gate section.
    
    Duplicate-dispatch note: tick code-factory-docs-2026-11-04-06-11-13 fired twice.
    The earlier session landed CF-166 (the CRIER_URL create-path contract, impl
